WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:06.340
Every protein starts as a gene,
copied into a message: messenger RNA.

2
00:00:06.390 --> 00:00:11.020
Once it leaves the nucleus, one
message can be translated many times.

3
00:00:11.070 --> 00:00:14.230
Humans have about 20 thousand genes.

4
00:00:14.280 --> 00:00:17.210
Yet they code for many
more proteins than that.

5
00:00:17.260 --> 00:00:20.250
So once a gene has been
copied into a message,

6
00:00:20.300 --> 00:00:23.660
can the cell still stop
its protein being made?

7
00:00:23.710 --> 00:00:27.540
In this mission, you'll follow
a message from gene to ribosome,

8
00:00:27.590 --> 00:00:29.180
step by step.

9
00:00:29.230 --> 00:00:31.790
Then you'll test your
answer on a new case,

10
00:00:31.840 --> 00:00:34.080
in a cell you have not met yet.

11
00:00:34.130 --> 00:00:39.060
Your mission: find out whether a cell
can still stop a protein once its message

12
00:00:39.110 --> 00:00:39.970
exists.
